{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["And the sons of Korah: Assir and Elkanah — because it is written before us: ״ובני קרח לא מתו״. ״ובני אהרן״ — on account of what is written: ״ואל משה אמר עלה אל ה' אתה ואהרן נדב ואביהוא״."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {0 "The comment addresses two lemmas from Exodus 6:24. The second sentence, beginning ובני אהרן, explains why Scripture then lists Aaron's sons: because of the juxtaposition in Exodus 24:1. The connective על שם שכתוב ('on account of what is written') links the listing of Aaron's sons to that earlier verse."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:40:34.015521483Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}